[1.187,"o","$ gitmancer help\n"]
[1.207,"o","\n⚡ gitmancer v0.5.0 — AI agent for your code & your whole GitHub account\n\n"]
[1.183,"o","USAGE\n  gitmancer <command> [args] [flags]\n\nCOMMANDS\n  setup                  store AI key + GitHub token locally (~/.gitmancer/config.json)\n                    --preset groq|openai|openrouter|zai|ollama|custom  --key  --token  --model  --base\n  config                 show current config (secrets masked)\n  whoami                 verify GitHub token — who are you on GitHub? --json\n  repos                  list your repositories           --limit 50  --json\n  ask \"<task>\"           AI agent: reads/writes code, runs commands, calls GitHub\n                    --yolo (skip confirmations)  --chat (stay in conversation)  --fast (small model)  --steps 50  --cwd <dir>  --budget 200000\n  fix \"<cmd>\"            run a command; if it fails, the agent auto-fixes the code & re-verifies\n                    --yolo  --fast  --cwd <dir>\n  ship [\"message\"]       stage all, AI commit message (if omitted), push current branch\n                    --no-push (commit locally only)\n  newrepo <name>         create GitHub repo + optionally push a folder in one shot\n                    --private  --source <dir>  --desc \"…\"  --m \"initial commit msg\"  --template node-lib\n  issue <owner/repo> …   list | create \"Title\" [--body \"…\"] | close <number> | reopen <number>\n                    --state all|open|closed  --limit N  --json\n  pr                    open a pull request — AI drafts title & body from your commits\n                    --base main  --head <branch>  --repo owner/name  --title \"…\"  --body \"…\"  --yolo\n  pr list                list pull requests                --state all|open|closed|merged  --repo owner/name  --json\n  pr close <n>           close a pull request              --repo owner/name  --yolo\n  pr merge <n>           merge a PR — confirm-gated        --squash  --rebase  --subject \"…\"  --repo owner/name\n  status                 dashboard: branch, dirty files, ahead/behind, open issues/PRs, last CI run\n                    --repo owner/name  --json\n  review <pr#>           AI code review of a pull request — severity-tagged findings + verdict\n                    --repo owner/name  --fast\n  sweep                 batch overview of ALL your repos — open issues/PRs per repo, 5-at-a-time\n                    --limit 30  --json\n  doctor                 diagnose setup: keys, tokens, endpoints, fallbacks — tells you what to fix\n  memory                 create/show GITMANCER.md — project rules auto-loaded into every AI run\n  undo [n]               revert the last n agent file changes (journal-based, default 1)\n  watch \"<cmd>\"          run a command; on failure the agent auto-fixes and re-runs until green\n                    --max 3  --yolo  --fast\n  prbot                 watch a repo and AI-review every new pull request\n                    --repo owner/name  --interval 300  --once  --yolo\n  changelog [from]      AI release notes for a commit range (default: since last tag)\n                    --to HEAD  --write (CHANGELOG.md)  --json\n  release patch|minor|major\n                    bump version + CHANGELOG + tag + push + GitHub release  --no-push  --skip-gh  --dry-run\n  secscan               scan tracked files (or --staged) for API keys & secrets — exit 1 if found\n                    --staged  --path <p>  --json\n  testgen <file>        AI-generates unit tests for a source file (dry preview; --write to save)\n                    --write  --yolo  --fast\n  explain <target>      AI explains a file, a git rev/range, or a shell command\n                    explain app.js · explain HEAD~1..HEAD · explain \"git rebase --onto\"\n  fleet <action>        run one action across every repo directly under --root\n                    status | pull | secscan | run \"<cmd>\"   --root <dir>  --json\n  triage <owner/repo>   AI triage of open issues — priority/type/label + rationale\n                    --apply (write labels)  --limit 20  --json  --yolo\n  hook list|install|uninstall [name]\n                    managed git hooks that run secscan — pre-commit (default) | pre-push | commit-msg  --force\n  plugin list|new|remove       manage plugins in ~/.gitmancer/plugins — custom commands + AI tools, no fork\n                    list [--json] · new <name> [--force] · remove <name> [--yolo] · path\n  mcp                   run as an MCP server (stdio JSON-RPC) — expose gitmancer tools to IDEs & agents\n                    read-only by default · GITMANCER_MCP_ALLOW_RUN=1 lifts the run gate\n  completions bash|zsh|fish  print a shell completion script — source it or drop it in your completion dir\n  record \"<cmd>\"          run a command, live + saved as an asciinema .cast session\n                    --out <file>   (stderr is merged into the recording)\n  replay [<file>|--list]    replay a recorded session (or any asciinema v2 cast)\n                    --speed 2  --list\n  help / version\n\nPROVIDERS\n  any OpenAI-compatible API works — set once in setup:\n    groq (free) · openai · openrouter · zai · ollama (local) · custom base URL\n\nSAFETY\n  tokens live only in ~/.gitmancer/config.json (chmod 600) — never uploaded, never logged.\n  writes / commands / GitHub mutations ask before acting, unless --yolo.\n\nEXAMPLES\n  gitmancer ask \"what does this repo do? then fix the typo in README\"\n  gitmancer ask --yolo --steps 50 \"add tests for utils.js and run them\"\n  gitmancer fix \"npm test\"                # tests failing? the agent repairs code & re-verifies\n  gitmancer pr --base main                # AI-drafted PR from your current branch\n  gitmancer pr list --state all --json    # full PR inventory for scripts\n  gitmancer pr merge 12 --squash          # confirm-gated merge\n  gitmancer review 12                     # AI code review: findings + verdict\n  gitmancer status                        # branch, sync, issues/PRs, CI — one shot\n  gitmancer sweep --json | jq '.[].repo'  # all repos, scriptable\n  gitmancer doctor                        # is my setup broken? what exactly?\n  gitmancer ship --no-push                # AI commit message, stay local\n  gitmancer newrepo my-lib --template node-lib --source ./my-lib\n  gitmancer issue me/myrepo create \"Bug: login fails on Safari\"\n  gitmancer secscan --staged             # block secrets before they're committed\n  gitmancer hook install pre-commit      # enforce secscan on every commit\n  gitmancer triage me/myrepo --apply     # AI-prioritize issues & label them\n  gitmancer explain HEAD~1..HEAD         # what did this change just do?\n  gitmancer fleet status --root ~/code   # every repo under ~/code at a glance\n  gitmancer plugin new hello             # scaffold a plugin → gitmancer hello just works\n\n\nPLUGINS (1 command from ~/.gitmancer/plugins)\n  banner <text>  — plugin demo: shouts text in a box\n\n"]
